{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #404: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. For which integers $a\\geq 1$ and primes $p$ is there a finite upper bound on those $k$ such that there are $a=a_1<\\cdots<a_n$ with\\[p^k \\mid (a_1!+\\cdots+a_n!)?\\]If $f(a,p)$ is the greatest such $k$, how does this function behave?\n\nIs there a prime $p$ and an infinite sequence $a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ such that if $p^{m_k}$ is the highest power of $p$ dividing $\\sum_{i\\leq k}a_i!$ then $m_k\\to \\infty$? Prize: no. Tags: factorials, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_004be58531fe3f03a5166463ef009f5b4563c9ae6a2e171696965723765e2c11","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:404","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_421956e0c1d5131e","object_root":"sha256:86de4c2fb56296d0b79973f8e9687df5c64c95c1536ee82e1e93b76b3997718c","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:404"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}